# /etc/chrony/sources.d/upstream.sources  --  LEAF
#
# NOSELECT IS DELIBERATE. These are monitored so `chronyc sources` can show how
# far the rig has drifted from UTC, but they can never be SELECTED, so they
# cannot steer this clock.
#
# Do NOT remove `noselect`, and do NOT add a pool here. A leaf with its own
# upstream is a second independent time base inside one recording. If it then
# disagrees with the rest of the rig, the discrepancy shows up as data that looks
# wrong rather than time that is wrong, and you debug the wrong thing.

server frd-gsw.hvl.no iburst noselect
server 128.39.103.52  iburst noselect
